<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rangin Mahal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">16th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rangin Mahal, or 'coloured palace', is a palace inside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidar">Bidar</a> Fort in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, built in the 16th century under the Barid Shahi sultans, mainly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-barid-shah-i">Ali Barid Shah I</a>. It is known for its carved wooden columns, coloured tilework and panels of mother-of-pearl inlaid in black stone.</p></div>
